                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire. Balliol
                        College (Domus de Balliolo). </orgName><p>Mynors (Balliol, 29) sets out the
                        evidence for connection to the Cistercian abbey of Builwas,
                        Shropshire.‘Donum Willelmi Gray’ (Langbaine)‘On 118v are two notes of
                        pledging: (a) Caucio magistri Thomas Chase posita in cista Turbewyle in
                        octavis sancti Laurencii pro vi s (?) viii d. A.D. Millesiomo cccc.mo
                        vicesimo quarto ; (b) Caucio magistri Thome Chase exposita in cista
                        Turbevyle in festo sancti Johannis ante portam latinam A.D. millesimo cccco
                        xxv. et habet supplementum unam peciam argenteam ponderis 1 unc. et di. in
                        cuius fundo scribitur rota sancte Katerine et iacet pro xxvi s. viii d.’
                        (Mynors, Balliol, 29)</p><p>See also under BUILDWAS, Shropshire, Savigniac
                        and (1147) Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St
                     Chad</p></provenance>
